{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## LIVE VALIDATION — attempted against the deployed endpoint. **PRE-FIX reproduction confirmed; the new AC is NOT satisfied and its box stays UNTICKED.**\n\n**Tool called:** `fsck`\n**Arguments:** `{}` (no arguments; `recover` left at its default `false`)\n**Endpoint:** the deployed rebar MCP server this session is connected to\n**When:** 2026-08-27, against the live shared store\n\n**Actual response — an ERROR object, verbatim:**\n\n```json\n{\"error\": \"command_failed\", \"input\": \"\", \"exit_code\": 1,\n \"message\": \"rebar fsck failed (exit 1): STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED: 218e-0ec1-385d-493a — concurrent claim/status race resolved (dropped uuid=968473b9-c90d-4c2f-88a7-a38bf3ce43b8)\\nSTATUS_FORK_RESOLVED: 3b78-de05-a125-418f — …\\nSTATUS_FORK_RESOLVED: 3e3f-8236-d619-43d7 — …\\nSTATUS_FORK_RESOLVED: 4214-ac28-d19c-41b9 — …\\nSTATUS_FORK_RESOLVED: 8ed5-9c7d-cb86-42c8 — …\\nSTATUS_FORK_RESOLVED: b043-9490-32ca-4548 — …\\nSTATUS_FORK_RESOLVED: fc9e-8c2e-cb2f-465f — …\\nORPHAN_EVENT: 79ef-23b3-04f2-42d2/1787486680190948001-…-COMMENT.json — pre-snapshot event not captured in source_event_uuids\\nORPHAN_EVENT: 8c8a-2756-ecfa-4b90/…-LINK.json — …\\nORPHAN_EVENT: cf34-9b8b-1aa7-4d95/…-LINK.json — …\\nORPHAN_EVENT: e042-4780-6c63-4b09/…-EDIT.json — …\\nENV_ID_MISMATCH: this environment ('eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f') has also written events under 2 other environment id(s) (ad49f17f-…, b2b5c498-…) — …\\nensures: 9/9 applied\\nauthorship: 31707 signed, 17760 unsigned event(s) — run `rebar verify-authorship`\\nfsck complete: 12 issues found\"}\n```\n\n**This is the BUG reproducing live, not the fix working.** It matches the original report\nexactly — 12 findings (7 `STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED`, 4 `ORPHAN_EVENT`, 1 `ENV_ID_MISMATCH`),\nnewline-joined into a single `message` string inside an `error` object, with no way for a client\nto enumerate them. The container is still serving the pre-fix build; the change is committed\nlocally and has not been landed or deployed.\n\n**Status of the new criterion: PENDING DEPLOYMENT.** The box is deliberately left unticked — a\npassing local test is not evidence, and I have not deployed anything. Re-run this exact call\nafter the change lands and the container redeploys; the expected post-fix response is a\nstructured object, i.e. `{\"issues\": [{\"kind\": \"status_fork_resolved\", \"ticket_id\":\n\"218e-0ec1-385d-493a\", \"detail\": \"…\"}, …], \"fixed\": [], \"issue_count\": …, \"returncode\": 1}`.\n\n### Two things this live store tells us that the local fixtures could not\n\n1. **The AC4 change does not mask real damage on this store.** 7 of the 12 findings are\n   self-healed `STATUS_FORK_RESOLVED`. After the change those stop counting, so the counted\n   tally drops from 12 to 5 — but `ORPHAN_EVENT` ×4 and `ENV_ID_MISMATCH` are genuine, still\n   counted, and this store still exits 1. Uncounting the self-healed class narrows the signal;\n   it does not silence it. That is the outcome the AC4 decision predicted, now observed on real\n   data.\n2. **The \"permanently failing\" claim is real, at scale.** Seven distinct tickets on the shared\n   store carry a permanent resolved-fork record. Since `status_fork_resolutions` never clears,\n   this store's `fsck` could never have returned 0 again — exactly the constant-signal failure\n   mode the decision comment argued from.\n\n### Plan-review attestation\n\n`plan_review_status` reports `{\"ok\": false, \"verdict\": \"unsigned\", \"reason\": \"no certified\nplan-review attestation (signature: unsigned; ticket has no signature)\"}`. This is not\n`stale-material` from the description edit — there was never a signed attestation to go stale:\nthe earlier `review_plan` run returned INDETERMINATE and therefore did not sign, because the\nLLM layer could not run on the server (`\"llm_error\": \"a bedrock model/provider is configured but\nthe optional bedrock provider package is not installed\"`). Its 11 deterministic checks all\npassed with zero blocking findings. Re-running would hit the same missing provider package, so\nit would consume 15-20 minutes and still return unsigned. Recorded rather than repeated. The\n`claim` succeeded without an attestation and **without any force override**, so nothing is being\nbypassed.\n"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787861293581220887,"uuid":"8e7c1224-a929-48e8-a599-109bb4079ae5"}